1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,646
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:30,905
[Anna] <i>Do you know how long I've</i>
<i>waited for this opportunity?</i>

6
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:33,074
[Ivy] <i>We are not murderers!</i>

7
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:36,202
<i>If you want justice,</i>
<i>then learn to cooperate.</i>

8
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:38,496
[Ivy] <i>I have information.</i>

9
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,957
<i>And I know that you'll be interested.</i>

10
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:45,211
[Emilia] <i>I will tear that woman</i>
<i>into pieces.</i>

11
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:50,049
<i>I'd like you to refrain from</i>
<i>refiling charges against Arnaldo.</i>

12
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:53,678
[Diego] <i>Arnaldo will pay</i>
<i>for all his crimes,</i>

13
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:54,846
<i>whether he likes it or not.</i>

14
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:57,891
[Ivy] <i>If you kill her, I won't</i>
<i>help you clean up her body.</i>

15
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:00,268
[Emilia] <i>If you sleep</i>
<i>with my husband again,</i>

16
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:01,519
<i>I will kill you.</i>

17
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,813
<i>Why don't you sponsor my candidacy?</i>

18
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:06,149
<i>Maybe someday, we could be running mates.</i>

19
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:08,359
<i>Why should I enter politics?</i>

20
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:09,778
<i>It has its own perks.</i>

21
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:13,281
<i>And you can actually steal</i>
<i>billions of money.</i> [laughs]

22
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>Oh, shoot.</i>

23
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:15,742
<i>Billions?</i>

24
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:19,496
[Camia] <i>You served as Emilia's secretary</i>

25
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:20,830
<i>when she was still mayor.</i>

26
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:24,042
<i>-I was hoping you could help me.</i>
-[Cora] <i>I'm sorry.</i>

27
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:25,752
-[Emilia] <i>Cheater!</i>
-[Raul] <i>Let's talk this through.</i>

28
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,086
-[Emilia] <i>Enough talk, Raul!</i>
-[Raul] <i>Please, stop.</i>

29
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:29,923
[Emilia] <i>We're over!</i>
<i>You get out of my life!</i>

30
00:01:30,006 --> 00:01:31,758
[Camia] <i>We're victims of</i>
<i>the Ardientes too.</i>

31
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:35,887
<i>I'm doing this so that one day,</i>
<i>the citizens of this town</i>

32
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,639
<i>can break free</i>
<i>from the Ardientes' tyranny.</i>

33
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:38,807
-[Arnaldo] <i>Ivy.</i>
-[nurse] <i>Mayor?</i>

34
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:40,934
[Arnaldo] <i>Stay there! Don't come near me!</i>

35
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:42,519
[nurse] <i>Mayor, no!</i>

36
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:43,728
[Arnaldo groaning]

37
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:45,605
[ominous music]

38
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:52,070
I used to work as Emilia's secretary
during her term as mayor.

39
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:56,533
And, yes, she did engage
in corrupt activities.

40
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:04,207
Miss Cora, thank you for trusting me
with this information.

41
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:09,671
But I think it's better
if I take you to a safe house.

42
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:14,050
We can speak more freely there.
Is that okay with you?

43
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:18,304
[suspenseful music playing]

44
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:23,017
[nurse] Mayor? Mayor?

45
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:27,897
Nurse?! Nurse! Nurse!

46
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:32,235
Help! Help us! Nurse! Help us! Guard!

47
00:02:32,318 --> 00:02:34,362
Guard! Guard!

48
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:38,241
[ominous music]

49
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:43,413
-[Diego] Auntie Camia!
-[Camia] Diego.

50
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:49,002
You and Miss Cora head inside.
I'll follow.

51
00:02:49,085 --> 00:02:50,086
All right.

52
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,505
-[Camia] Please follow them.
-Come in, Miss Cora.

53
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:00,889
Please, have a seat.

54
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:07,687
[Cora] Thank you.

55
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:12,525
[car arriving]

56
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,665
-Mom.
-Lily.

57
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,925
Are you ready to hear
the witness' testimony?

58
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,760
I'm ready, Mom.

59
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:43,723
This will be a big help
in taking Emilia down.

60
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:46,267
Come on.

61
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:53,149
-I'll go on ahead.
-Okay.

62
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:04,285
-Auntie.
-Thank you.

63
00:04:07,705 --> 00:04:09,040
So, Miss Cora…

64
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:12,085
Let's start.

65
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:18,800
[suspenseful music playing]

66
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:26,557
[confused] Miss Camia, is that a recorder?

67
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:29,852
Are you recording this conversation?

68
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:32,647
Uh…

69
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:40,113
When did you start working
as Emilia Ardiente's secretary?

70
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:43,908
I started working for her in 2004.

71
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:49,122
Mrs. Emilia was the mayor at the time.

72
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:52,458
<i>Even then, the Ardientes</i>
<i>were such extravagant people.</i>

73
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:56,462
<i>That was the time when they had</i>

74
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:59,340
<i>Señor Julio's statue erected.</i>

75
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:04,804
They were able to extort a lot
of money out of that project.

76
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:07,140
<i>They got almost triple…</i>

77
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:10,810
…the amount of the
government's original budget.

78
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:19,027
But then, their worst act of corruption…

79
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:25,408
was when Mrs. Emilia
founded the Women's Union.

80
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:28,161
[tense music playing]

81
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:30,204
The Women's Union?

82
00:05:33,207 --> 00:05:35,752
Are you sure I won't
get in trouble for this?

83
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:37,253
[Camia] <i>No, Miss Cora.</i>

84
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,797
We promise to protect you

85
00:05:39,881 --> 00:05:42,341
if you testify against the Ardientes.

86
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:44,552
What? Testify?!

87
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:47,638
You didn't say anything about that.

88
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,976
[sullen music playing]

89
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:58,441
[phone vibrating]

90
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:04,322
Emilia.

91
00:06:04,989 --> 00:06:07,909
Hello, Ivy? Where are you?

92
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:10,369
Why? What's wrong?

93
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:13,581
You need to come here
to the hospital. Arnaldo's gone.

94
00:06:13,664 --> 00:06:14,832
[dramatic music]

95
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,043
What?!

96
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:23,841
Emilia, stay right there.
I'll be on my way. Wait for me.

97
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:31,891
[phone rings]

98
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,601
Excuse me.

99
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:39,565
Mom, I have to go.
Something happened to Arnaldo.

100
00:06:39,649 --> 00:06:40,566
What?

101
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,569
He's gone missing.
We can't let this happen.

102
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:46,030
We still need him for our plans.

103
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:49,867
-Okay, keep us updated.
-I will, Mom.

104
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:54,539
[tense music playing]

105
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,707
[Ivy] Come on. Hurry, let's go.

106
00:07:06,217 --> 00:07:11,097
Please don't worry, Miss Cora.
We're here to protect you.

107
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,726
[sullen music playing]

108
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:25,570
I think it was a mistake coming here.

109
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:27,822
[Cora] I'm sorry.

110
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:30,575
-Miss Cora?
-Miss Cora.

111
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:32,952
[Camia] Miss Cora!

112
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:37,790
Let's just leave her alone
for now and try again tomorrow.

113
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,876
It'll be harder if we force her.

114
00:07:40,877 --> 00:07:43,880
[dramatic music playing]

115
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:54,015
-[Ivy] What happened?!
-Ivy.

116
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:56,142
I was on my way
to visit Arnaldo in his room,

117
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:58,144
but he was no longer there!

118
00:07:58,227 --> 00:07:59,729
What, how? What do you mean?

119
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:03,107
The nurses said they found
the room empty. He's missing!

120
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:04,734
But how could that have happened?!

121
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:06,486
I don't know!

122
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,321
Does Congressman know?

123
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:09,864
[panics] I'll call him.

124
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:15,244
[phone ringing]

125
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:21,876
Hello.

126
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:23,878
Papa?

127
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:25,922
<i>It's Arnaldo. He's gone.</i>

128
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:30,134
What? What?!

129
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:35,640
[dramatic music playing]

130
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:41,562
Arnaldo! Arnaldo, come out!
Where did you go?

131
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:42,647
-Emilia…
-Arnaldo!

132
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,315
-Emilia!
-Don't just stand there.

133
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:46,484
Find him! Arnaldo!

134
00:08:46,567 --> 00:08:47,860
Can you calm down?

135
00:08:47,944 --> 00:08:49,403
What if you get hospitalized next?

136
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:52,865
Don't act like you're
the most miserable person

137
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:55,117
on the planet. I'm sure we'll find him!

138
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,786
But where?! We can't find him.

139
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:58,371
-I'm palpitating!
-Just relax!

140
00:08:58,454 --> 00:09:00,164
[Emilia] Arnaldo, come out!

141
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:01,999
[Arnaldo murmuring]
They thought they could kill me.

142
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,125
But they can't.

143
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:04,210
[man 1] Here.

144
00:09:05,461 --> 00:09:07,380
-[man 2] It's the mayor!
-[man 3] It's the mayor!

145
00:09:07,463 --> 00:09:08,798
They can't kill me. They thought…

146
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:12,009
Mayor Arnaldo, is that you?
It really is him!

147
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:13,970
Let go of me! Let go of me!

148
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:15,263
Don't come near me! You can't control me!

149
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:16,806
[man 1] Mayor come with us, please.

150
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:17,932
Let go of me!

151
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:20,268
-[man 1] Mayor, please.
-Let go of me.

152
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:21,852
Didn't I tell you to let go of me?!

153
00:09:21,936 --> 00:09:24,564
-[screaming] Mayor! Stop!
-Mayor!

154
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,482
-Mayor!
-Mayor!

155
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,858
Mayor!

156
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,068
-[cop 1] Ma'am!
-[Emilia] What?

157
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:32,572
-[cop 1] It's the mayor!
-[Emilia] What?!

158
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:34,323
-[cop 2] Come on, let's go!
-Where is he?

159
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:36,367
-[cop 2] Here.
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!

160
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:38,828
Mayor! Mayor!

161
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:40,621
-[Emilia] What's happening?!
-[Arnaldo] You can't kill me!

162
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:42,415
-[cop 3] Mayor!
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!

163
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:44,166
-Arnaldo, stop it!
-Hon!

164
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,252
[Emilia] Stop it! [exclaims]

165
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:47,336
[cop 3] Mayor!

166
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:49,338
[Emilia gasping]

167
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:52,008
Arnaldo!

168
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:56,387
No! No! You can't pin me down!

169
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:57,471
[cop 1] That's enough!

170
00:09:57,930 --> 00:09:59,181
That's enough. [shushes]

171
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,892
[tense music playing]

172
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,358
[Arnaldo] Wait, where are you taking me?
I'm not crazy!

173
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:11,861
-Gently, please.
-I'm not crazy! Let me go!

174
00:10:11,944 --> 00:10:14,780
-Mayor! Mayor!
-Let me go! Now!

175
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:15,865
Okay.

176
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:18,034
[Arnaldo groaning]

177
00:10:20,911 --> 00:10:24,790
One of our nurses was badly
injured because of his outburst.

178
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:27,209
The mayor is dangerous,
that's why we moved him

179
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:28,919
to the psychiatric ward.

180
00:10:29,211 --> 00:10:31,881
This is Dr. Go, our psychiatrist.

181
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:35,134
She will take over
the case of Mayor Arnaldo.

182
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:36,844
Congressman?

183
00:10:37,219 --> 00:10:38,888
Doc, before anything else,

184
00:10:38,971 --> 00:10:41,724
I don't need any more negative reports.

185
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:45,645
All I want you to do
is to treat my grandson well

186
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:46,979
to the best of your abilities

187
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:49,315
so that he can be cured right away.

188
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:52,360
Pa, we have to know everything.

189
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:54,362
That's the only way we can help him.

190
00:10:56,238 --> 00:11:00,868
Mayor Arnaldo is showing
symptoms of bipolar I disorder.

191
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:04,622
Every time he goes through
a manic episode,

192
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:07,166
he experiences paranoia,

193
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:11,420
wherein he exhibits suicidal
and violent tendencies.

194
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:14,256
But we're giving him medication, doc.

195
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:16,384
Why does it seem like his condition

196
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:17,718
just keeps getting worse?

197
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:20,638
Well, his condition can
only be managed effectively by,

198
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:25,101
yes, medication, but he also
needs gradual therapy.

199
00:11:25,184 --> 00:11:27,978
In other words,
he really needs to take a rest.

200
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:31,107
And I strongly urge members of the family

201
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:33,609
to take an active role in his therapy

202
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:37,780
and to keep the mayor in a calm
and stress-free environment

203
00:11:37,863 --> 00:11:39,865
so he can fully recover.

204
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:41,867
[exhales]

205
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,626
[Jaguar] You can have the rest of it.

206
00:11:51,919 --> 00:11:54,130
And you, Madrigal, this is for you.

207
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:56,757
That's all yours.

208
00:11:57,925 --> 00:12:00,386
You did an excellent job. I'm impressed.

209
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:03,764
They should all learn from you.

210
00:12:06,934 --> 00:12:08,853
-Thank you.
-Thank you, boss.

211
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:11,856
[sighs]

212
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:13,774
Let's drink.

213
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:17,194
Cheers.

214
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:22,741
Jaguar.

215
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:29,832
What are you doing here, Natalie?

216
00:12:29,915 --> 00:12:33,419
Didn't I tell you never to come here?

217
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:39,675
Stay there.

218
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:43,596
Let me go!

219
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:47,892
Do you know what your wife did to me?

220
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:49,727
Huh?

221
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:52,354
This.

222
00:12:53,731 --> 00:12:56,692
So you better tell
that gorgeous wife of yours

223
00:12:58,277 --> 00:13:02,323
to never be in my way ever again.

224
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:08,496
Hold on, Natalie, who are you
to order me around?

225
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:11,582
You talk like you're all that.
Who do you think you are?

226
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:13,292
You're just someone I fool around with.

227
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:19,507
How dare you?!

228
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,510
Don't think so highly of yourself.

229
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:25,304
Let me just remind you,

230
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:28,224
I'm the reason why you were able
to get back up again.

231
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:35,189
Don't wait for the day that
I'll take back everything…

232
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:37,733
everything I gave you.

233
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:44,740
I will take back everything.

234
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:51,038
And, when I say, "everything,"
Jaguar, I mean <i>everything</i>.

235
00:13:52,581 --> 00:13:56,877
You will have nothing left.
Not even your soul.

236
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:05,344
-[dramatic music playing]
-[chuckles]

237
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:18,065
Grandpa…

238
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:21,277
please take this off me.

239
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:28,367
I'm all better now. I don't need this.

240
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:30,744
Just take me home. Come on.

241
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:35,791
This is a place for low-level nut cases.

242
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:39,003
Not for someone like Arnaldo Ardiente.

243
00:14:39,461 --> 00:14:40,671
Doctor, I'm very sorry,

244
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:44,842
but I think I will have to take
my grandson out of this place.

245
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:46,093
Arnaldo…

246
00:14:47,469 --> 00:14:48,596
you'll get better.

247
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:52,558
But not here. Not in this hellhole.

248
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:55,978
You will spend time in our rest house,

249
00:14:56,061 --> 00:15:00,983
where you will get fresh air,
a calm environment,

250
00:15:01,066 --> 00:15:04,111
and I promise you, you will have
nurses at your beck and call

251
00:15:04,194 --> 00:15:06,071
for anything you need.

252
00:15:06,697 --> 00:15:11,368
You will get well,
and you will win the election.

253
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:14,705
-[Julio sighs]
-[Arnaldo] Thank you. Thank you.

254
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:16,874
I… I promise I'll get better.

255
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:18,125
[Julio] Good.

256
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,882
But I have one request.

257
00:15:24,965 --> 00:15:27,259
Anything, anything. What is it?

258
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,472
I want Ivy to come with me.

259
00:15:31,555 --> 00:15:33,474
[dramatic music]

260
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:38,395
[suspenseful music playing]

261
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:49,740
I want her there every step of the way.

262
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:57,706
[tense music playing]

263
00:16:00,459 --> 00:16:03,504
Oh, Aunt Claire, Raul is so stubborn.

264
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:04,672
He keeps calling.

265
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:06,507
How many times do I have to tell him…

266
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:08,175
-[phone ringing]
-Here he goes again.

267
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:09,927
-That it's over between us?
-[phone ringing]

268
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:14,682
Well, what about your promise to Julio

269
00:16:14,765 --> 00:16:16,600
and the condition he gave you?

270
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:18,894
That you have to fix your marriage?

271
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,730
Or maybe you're still so stubborn

272
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:25,067
because you still have Jaguar
at your disposal.

273
00:16:25,734 --> 00:16:27,152
-[Claire] Well?
-[Julio] Emilia?

274
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:28,570
Papa.

275
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:32,825
I want you to visit Arnaldo more.

276
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:36,787
And, please, talk to his doctor also.

277
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:39,248
Tell him to increase
his visits to Arnaldo,

278
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:42,209
so that he may monitor him better.

279
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,920
-Yes, Papa.
-Okay.

280
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:49,717
But I'm surprised.
I thought you trusted Ivy Aguas.

281
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,137
That was before.

282
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:58,183
When I thought Arnaldo could come home.

283
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:04,481
But to send him away, alone,
with Miss Aguas?

284
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:08,402
That's another story.

285
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,613
Don't you get my drift?

286
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:16,952
I don't trust anyone.

287
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:19,872
Especially not when it comes
to my grandson.

288
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:21,707
Not you…

289
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:27,671
and most especially, not Miss Aguas.

290
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:32,426
Now… I'm going to my room.

291
00:17:37,973 --> 00:17:41,643
Mom, Arnaldo asked me to
come with him to his rest house.

292
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:45,856
Wait, Lily. I don't trust Arnaldo.

293
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:48,734
After hearing about his diagnosis?

294
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:51,195
He might go ballistic and hurt you.

295
00:17:51,278 --> 00:17:53,530
I can handle Arnaldo.

296
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:57,242
<i>Just let him try. He can't do anything.</i>

297
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:59,828
There are plenty of nurses and
bodyguards around to stop him.

298
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,791
I'm just worried
that I can't come with you

299
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:05,667
to talk to the witness.

300
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,504
That's what I'm worried about, dear.

301
00:18:09,213 --> 00:18:10,756
Miss Cora backed out.

302
00:18:11,715 --> 00:18:13,467
<i>But I won't give up on her.</i>

303
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:16,178
Our plans don't have a huge time frame.

304
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:20,682
[Julio] I hope I'm not interrupting.

305
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:28,232
No. No, Congressman.

306
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:33,737
Uh… I just wanted to thank you
for doing this.

307
00:18:34,029 --> 00:18:35,697
No need to thank me.

308
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:38,992
Because I really do want Arnaldo
to get better.

309
00:18:40,327 --> 00:18:41,328
Likewise.

310
00:18:42,454 --> 00:18:43,872
Just a reminder, Ivy.

311
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:50,254
Please, please, bring back
my grandson in one piece.

312
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:53,132
-Or else--
-No worries, Congressman.

313
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:56,760
I'll bring him back in
one piece, as per your request.

314
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:58,720
[chuckles]

315
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,851
[tense music playing]

316
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:06,228
Auntie?

317
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:14,153
Lily can't come with us
to visit Miss Cora.

318
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:17,197
Arnaldo has been discharged
from the hospital,

319
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:20,284
and they brought my daughter
with them to their rest house.

320
00:19:20,367 --> 00:19:24,913
[suspenseful music playing]

321
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:35,591
[ominous music]

322
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:18,884
[dramatic music playing]

323
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:45,702
[tense music playing]

324
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:52,167
Thank you.

325
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:00,717
Despite everything that happened…

326
00:21:02,135 --> 00:21:03,178
you're still here.

327
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:08,517
Thank you.

328
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:17,484
[tense music playing]

329
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:26,660
I love you.

330
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,085
[ominous music]

331
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:53,812
[line ringing]

332
00:21:54,438 --> 00:21:55,647
[phone vibrates]

333
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:57,482
Diego.

334
00:21:57,816 --> 00:21:58,817
[Diego] <i>Ivy.</i>

335
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:02,529
Whatever it is you're planning,
keep your guard up.

336
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:06,742
If you want to be alone,

337
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:08,994
there's a garden near the main house.

338
00:22:10,245 --> 00:22:11,246
Thank you.

339
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:13,915
[Diego] <i>That's where I used to go…</i>

340
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:16,043
when we were young.

341
00:22:16,793 --> 00:22:18,712
When you were still an Ardiente.

342
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:22,132
Ivy, you shouldn't have
let Arnaldo force you

343
00:22:22,215 --> 00:22:23,467
to go with him.

344
00:22:26,678 --> 00:22:28,013
It's actually for the better.

345
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:31,266
This way, I can carefully devise
my plan against Emilia.

346
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,769
<i>They won't suspect a thing because…</i>

347
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:35,771
I'm taking care of Arnaldo.

348
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:37,355
[Diego] <i>But, remember this.</i>

349
00:22:37,814 --> 00:22:40,776
If you offer your hand to the Ardientes,

350
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:43,111
they will take your whole arm.

351
00:22:44,112 --> 00:22:47,115
<i>If not, they will take</i>
<i>your body or your soul.</i>

352
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:49,451
They won't get anything from me.

353
00:22:51,536 --> 00:22:53,455
I have to go. Take care.

354
00:22:55,874 --> 00:22:57,292
-[ominous music]
-[Ivy gasps]

355
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:01,505
[tense music playing]

356
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:04,299
[stutters] Arnaldo.

357
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:06,343
Who were you talking to?

358
00:23:09,596 --> 00:23:11,139
-Who were you talking to?
-[nurse] Excuse me.

359
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:12,099
[nurse] Mayor?

360
00:23:12,182 --> 00:23:13,016
-Yes?
-[nurse] Please come here.

361
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:14,434
-I think…
-Time to take your medicine.

362
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,353
…you need to take your medicine.

363
00:23:16,436 --> 00:23:17,979
[Nimfa] <i>You shouldn't trust her.</i>

364
00:23:18,063 --> 00:23:18,939
What did you say?

365
00:23:19,022 --> 00:23:21,233
This way, please.
Time to take your medicine.

366
00:23:21,316 --> 00:23:22,484
-That's not what you said.
-Nothing, sir.

367
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:23,985
-What did you say?
-Time to take your medicine.

368
00:23:24,069 --> 00:23:25,362
-You said something. What?
-Nothing, sir.

369
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:27,781
[Nimfa] <i>She's the one feeding</i>
<i>information to Diego's camp.</i>

370
00:23:27,864 --> 00:23:29,241
-Did you hear that?
-There's nothing there.

371
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:30,242
Did you hear that?

372
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:31,493
[nurse] Here. Take your medicine.

373
00:23:31,576 --> 00:23:32,661
[Arnaldo] Did you hear that?

374
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:35,205
[Nimfa] <i>She's Diego's spy</i>
<i>within the Ardiente family!</i>

375
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:36,164
What?!

376
00:23:36,957 --> 00:23:37,999
[Arnaldo] There you go again!

377
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,085
-[Nimfa] <i>She's just using you!</i>
-What are you saying?!

378
00:23:40,168 --> 00:23:41,962
You didn't hear anything?
Are you saying I'm crazy?

379
00:23:42,045 --> 00:23:43,255
-No, sir.
-Arnaldo!

380
00:23:43,338 --> 00:23:44,798
-[nurse] Nurse! Nurse!
-[Arnaldo] I'm crazy?!

381
00:23:44,881 --> 00:23:46,383
-[Ivy] Arnaldo!
-[Nimfa] <i>You shouldn't trust her.</i>

382
00:23:46,466 --> 00:23:48,343
-[Ivy] Guards!
-[Nimfa] <i>She's just using you.</i>

383
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:49,678
-[Arnaldo] Who are you?
-[nurse] Take him inside.

384
00:23:49,761 --> 00:23:51,638
-Arnaldo, relax.
-[nurse] Take him inside, now!

385
00:23:51,721 --> 00:23:52,764
No! Ivy! I heard someone's voice!

386
00:23:52,848 --> 00:23:56,059
-Nurse!
-Go and take him to his room.

387
00:23:56,143 --> 00:23:56,935
What's that?

388
00:23:57,018 --> 00:23:58,353
-[Ivy] Arnaldo, relax. I'll--
-Ivy!

389
00:23:58,436 --> 00:23:59,229
[Ivy] Yes?

390
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:00,605
-I'll be with you soon.
-[Ivy] I'm fine!

391
00:24:00,689 --> 00:24:03,567
-I'm just hearing voices!
-I know, I know. I'm coming soon.

392
00:24:06,069 --> 00:24:09,072
[suspenseful music playing]

393
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:25,839
-[knocks on door]
-Anyone home?

394
00:24:27,215 --> 00:24:28,258
Miss Cora!

395
00:24:29,634 --> 00:24:31,136
Miss Cora!

396
00:24:31,219 --> 00:24:32,262
-Hello?
-Miss Cora?

397
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:34,723
-[Camia] Hello?
-It's locked. Is she in there?

398
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:37,809
[Camia] Anyone home?

399
00:24:37,893 --> 00:24:39,853
-Looking for Miss Cora?
-[Jepoy] Anybody home?

400
00:24:39,936 --> 00:24:42,647
Oh. Yes, we are. Have you seen her?

401
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:45,901
Ma'am, she left early this morning,
together with her kid.

402
00:24:45,984 --> 00:24:46,735
What?

403
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:49,779
-Do you know where they went?
-I don't.

404
00:24:49,863 --> 00:24:51,573
But they brought a lot of stuff with them.

405
00:24:51,656 --> 00:24:54,201
They're probably headed
to her nephew's place in Manila.

406
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:56,369
Manila? Do you know their address?

407
00:24:56,453 --> 00:25:00,207
I'm sorry, I don't. Excuse me.

408
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:03,960
Manila?

409
00:25:04,711 --> 00:25:05,921
Oh, god.

410
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:09,591
How are we ever going
to find Miss Cora there?

411
00:25:15,597 --> 00:25:16,932
[Dr. Go] Hallucinations.

412
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:21,186
This is a side effect of your condition.

413
00:25:21,269 --> 00:25:23,897
It starts with hearing voices
and continues

414
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:26,733
until it becomes
a full-blown hallucination.

415
00:25:26,816 --> 00:25:29,486
But if you continue your medication,

416
00:25:29,569 --> 00:25:31,738
the hallucinations will go away.

417
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:34,866
Where do these hallucinations come from?

418
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:37,994
[Dr. Go] Sometimes, there are truths

419
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:40,956
buried in our subconscious.

420
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:45,460
And when our
"unsettled business" resurfaces,

421
00:25:45,543 --> 00:25:49,214
it manifests in the form
of dreams or hallucinations.

422
00:25:50,090 --> 00:25:54,427
Why, Mayor?
Whose voice do you usually hear?

423
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:58,974
What are you trying to forget?

424
00:25:59,474 --> 00:26:00,934
Can we talk about it?

425
00:26:01,309 --> 00:26:02,978
[eerie music]

426
00:26:08,566 --> 00:26:10,568
[suspenseful music playing]

427
00:26:14,447 --> 00:26:15,448
Nothing, doc.

428
00:26:25,333 --> 00:26:28,336
[suspenseful music escalates]

429
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:33,383
By the way, guys.

430
00:26:33,466 --> 00:26:36,803
We are visiting the home
for the aged in a few days.

431
00:26:36,886 --> 00:26:38,388
This will be our first appearance,

432
00:26:38,471 --> 00:26:40,473
following Arnaldo's incident.

433
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:43,893
That's right. Batch, I'm sure
your campaign will be a success.

434
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:45,270
We don't really need to do anything

435
00:26:45,353 --> 00:26:47,230
because you've already
clobbered the competition.

436
00:26:47,314 --> 00:26:48,773
[Loring] I hope the mayor's sick leave

437
00:26:48,857 --> 00:26:50,317
lasts until the election ends.

438
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:51,735
[all laugh]

439
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:53,653
[Diego] Even so.

440
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:57,407
We still need to give it our all.

441
00:26:57,490 --> 00:27:00,577
Because that's what
our supporters deserve.

442
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:02,871
[Marlon] That's right. Miss Camia's here.

443
00:27:02,954 --> 00:27:05,498
[Loring] That's right, dream big.

444
00:27:06,833 --> 00:27:07,876
[Fernan laughing]

445
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:09,336
Auntie, Anna.

446
00:27:09,419 --> 00:27:10,920
-Diego.
-How did it go?

447
00:27:13,423 --> 00:27:15,425
Miss Cora's not in her house anymore.

448
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:18,636
But I won't let the investigation

449
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:22,015
on Emilia end here. I won't give up.

450
00:27:22,098 --> 00:27:25,602
Diego, I'm afraid of what might happen
in our next campaign.

451
00:27:25,685 --> 00:27:29,022
I feel the Ardientes
are watching our every move.

452
00:27:29,105 --> 00:27:31,858
Julio might even make good on his threat.

453
00:27:32,567 --> 00:27:33,735
Don't worry.

454
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:36,446
Let's just stay vigilant.

455
00:27:36,529 --> 00:27:39,115
We won't postpone the campaign.

456
00:27:39,199 --> 00:27:41,618
Besides, we have nothing to fear.

457
00:27:41,701 --> 00:27:42,702
We're not doing anything wrong.

458
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:44,829
In fact, they're the ones
who should be afraid.

459
00:27:45,455 --> 00:27:49,918
Because eventually, their victims
will come to get them.

460
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:51,544
-That's right, Diego.
-That's right.

461
00:27:52,212 --> 00:27:53,213
[Fernan] That's right.

462
00:27:53,838 --> 00:27:55,632
[Marlon] It's what they deserve.

463
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:58,093
[tense music playing]

464
00:28:05,850 --> 00:28:07,811
[eerie music playing]

465
00:28:08,228 --> 00:28:09,479
<i>Mayor Arnaldo!</i>

466
00:28:10,980 --> 00:28:13,733
<i>I need to tell her something</i>
<i>about Miss Ivy.</i>

467
00:28:14,609 --> 00:28:16,903
<i>You shouldn't trust her.</i>

468
00:28:16,986 --> 00:28:19,739
<i>She's the one feeding</i>
<i>information to Diego's camp!</i>

469
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:20,740
[Arnaldo] <i>That's not true.</i>

470
00:28:20,824 --> 00:28:23,368
<i>She's Diego's spy</i>
<i>within the Ardiente family!</i>

471
00:28:23,451 --> 00:28:25,578
-<i>She's just using you.</i>
-[Arnaldo] <i>That's not true!</i>

472
00:28:25,662 --> 00:28:27,414
[Nimfa] <i>Mayor, you need to know</i>
<i>that Ivy is?</i>

473
00:28:27,497 --> 00:28:31,209
-<i>That's not true!</i> [screams]
-[gunshots]

474
00:28:31,626 --> 00:28:33,253
[ominous music]

475
00:28:39,592 --> 00:28:41,594
[eerie music]

476
00:29:03,867 --> 00:29:05,744
[eerie music]

477
00:29:11,875 --> 00:29:12,876
[ominous music]

478
00:29:17,964 --> 00:29:20,967
[eerie music playing]

479
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:44,699
[ominous music]

480
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:57,378
[dramatic music playing]

481
00:30:07,847 --> 00:30:10,225
[tense music]

482
00:30:17,857 --> 00:30:20,902
[Arnaldo] <i>You shouldn't trust Ivy Aguas.</i>

483
00:30:23,446 --> 00:30:28,201
<i>She's been lying to you.</i>
<i>You shouldn't trust that woman.</i>

484
00:30:30,578 --> 00:30:32,455
[tense music playing]

485
00:30:50,974 --> 00:30:52,976
[dramatic music playing]

486
00:31:04,070 --> 00:31:06,072
[tense music playing]

487
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:25,592
[birds chirping]

488
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:34,976
Jenny?

489
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:36,603
[clears throat]

490
00:31:36,686 --> 00:31:37,854
-[Emilia] Jenny!
-Emilia.

491
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:42,859
Emilia, wait.

492
00:31:44,193 --> 00:31:47,322
-What are you doing here?
-I was waiting for you.

493
00:31:47,822 --> 00:31:51,492
Haven't I made myself clear?
I still remember it.

494
00:31:51,576 --> 00:31:54,913
I said we were over. You should leave.

495
00:31:54,996 --> 00:31:56,956
Emilia, wait. Let's talk about this.

496
00:31:58,333 --> 00:31:59,626
You made your point.

497
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:02,629
You're right. I shouldn't be lying to you.

498
00:32:02,795 --> 00:32:05,882
But Natalie's the one who went after me.

499
00:32:07,592 --> 00:32:08,468
Want an award?

500
00:32:08,843 --> 00:32:10,386
But I didn't do anything with her.

501
00:32:10,845 --> 00:32:12,889
I rejected her because I love you.

502
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:18,478
And where did your chase end?

503
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:19,854
On the bed?

504
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:22,231
You're my wife.
You're the one I love, Emilia.

505
00:32:22,315 --> 00:32:26,152
I left her. Let's work this out.

506
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:35,787
Guards? Escort this man outside.

507
00:32:35,870 --> 00:32:38,706
And make sure he never comes back here.

508
00:32:39,540 --> 00:32:40,541
Emilia.

509
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:55,181
[slow instrumental playing]

510
00:33:07,193 --> 00:33:08,194
[giggles]

511
00:33:10,196 --> 00:33:11,698
[whispers] Payback time.

512
00:33:23,084 --> 00:33:25,086
[suspenseful music playing]

513
00:33:33,261 --> 00:33:34,220
[door opens]

514
00:33:42,437 --> 00:33:43,438
[door closes]

515
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:55,283
How was your sleep?

516
00:33:58,077 --> 00:33:59,203
Mine was great.

517
00:34:01,330 --> 00:34:04,667
The doctor's medicine is helping my mood.

518
00:34:07,879 --> 00:34:09,630
Somebody went into my room.

519
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:18,139
Could be the nurses or the maids.

520
00:34:20,850 --> 00:34:22,769
There are too many people in this house.

521
00:34:22,852 --> 00:34:24,854
Do you want me to call them all here?

522
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:27,940
No.

523
00:34:28,858 --> 00:34:29,859
It's okay.

524
00:34:30,693 --> 00:34:34,572
I'll just make sure whoever
did it can't do it again.

525
00:34:34,739 --> 00:34:35,823
[ominous music]

526
00:34:43,289 --> 00:34:45,750
If I went into your room…

527
00:34:49,921 --> 00:34:51,172
would that be okay?

528
00:34:58,679 --> 00:34:59,680
Arnaldo.

529
00:35:03,351 --> 00:35:04,310
[sighs]

530
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:08,439
Are you doing anything today?

531
00:35:10,066 --> 00:35:12,276
I'm in the mood for a swim.

532
00:35:13,236 --> 00:35:17,240
I need to go to Manila.
I have to go to my head office.

533
00:35:17,615 --> 00:35:19,117
I have some work to do.

534
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:22,078
[exhales]

535
00:35:22,995 --> 00:35:23,996
Sure.

536
00:35:25,039 --> 00:35:27,166
But the bodyguards aren't here.
I sent them off.

537
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:29,168
Nobody will bring you there.

538
00:35:29,836 --> 00:35:32,922
It's okay. I know how to drive.

539
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:37,260
[tense music playing]

540
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:53,651
[dramatic music playing]

541
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:17,758
[Ivy] <i>I know that was you, Arnaldo.</i>

542
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:20,887
<i>What's going on in your head, you monster?</i>

543
00:36:27,685 --> 00:36:29,228
[ominous music]

544
00:36:36,903 --> 00:36:38,779
[inner voice] <i>No.</i>

545
00:36:41,657 --> 00:36:46,913
<i>Ivy Aguas can't leave</i>
<i>because you can't trust her.</i>

546
00:36:49,207 --> 00:36:51,209
No! There you go again!

547
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:53,794
There you go again! Stop it!

548
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:55,796
-Stop it!
-[inner voice] <i>Calm down.</i>

549
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:58,633
You are sick! No! No!

550
00:36:58,716 --> 00:37:02,470
-[inner voice] <i>She can't leave.</i>
-Don't listen to him!

551
00:37:02,553 --> 00:37:05,848
No! You're taking over.
You're not taking over.

552
00:37:05,932 --> 00:37:08,893
No! No! No! No!

553
00:37:09,852 --> 00:37:10,937
[eerie sound]

554
00:37:11,812 --> 00:37:13,105
[panting]

555
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:15,858
What do you want? This?

556
00:37:15,942 --> 00:37:19,487
Let's stop this. You're too noisy.

557
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:21,822
I'm going to end this. Right now!

558
00:37:24,575 --> 00:37:25,701
See?

559
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:29,914
[tutting]

560
00:37:30,665 --> 00:37:31,707
Don't do it.

561
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:34,961
Don't do it.

562
00:37:38,839 --> 00:37:40,716
You know, sometimes,
I think Grandpa is right.

563
00:37:41,717 --> 00:37:42,802
You're weak.

564
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:47,098
Now, let me take over.

565
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:51,686
And I'll take care of business.

566
00:37:51,769 --> 00:37:53,854
I'll take care of her for you.

567
00:37:55,856 --> 00:37:56,857
For us.

568
00:37:59,443 --> 00:38:00,444
Okay?

569
00:38:01,821 --> 00:38:03,698
I'm going to finish this.

570
00:38:04,657 --> 00:38:05,783
[razor clatters on floor]

571
00:38:05,866 --> 00:38:06,867
[dramatic music]

572
00:38:09,578 --> 00:38:11,372
If Arnaldo really is all right,

573
00:38:11,455 --> 00:38:13,791
then why isn't he making an appearance?

574
00:38:13,874 --> 00:38:15,876
Where is he really?

575
00:38:16,585 --> 00:38:21,215
He's okay, okay? What else have you heard?

576
00:38:21,716 --> 00:38:24,885
[woman 2] That he and Ivy Aguas
are getting married again!

577
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:28,806
Apparently, they eloped.
Someone saw them in Tagaytay.

578
00:38:28,889 --> 00:38:30,850
So, is it true?

579
00:38:31,600 --> 00:38:32,727
Well, that's true.

580
00:38:32,810 --> 00:38:35,229
They're having their alone time now.

581
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:37,356
Can we not talk about them? What else?

582
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:38,941
What other rumors have you heard?

583
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:41,777
[woman 3] How about Raul?
How is your annulment going?

584
00:38:42,445 --> 00:38:43,779
You know, just eat.

585
00:38:43,863 --> 00:38:45,406
You're making me lose my appetite.

586
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:46,866
[women chuckling]

587
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:51,620
Oh.

588
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:54,498
-[Jerry] Wait!
-Oh! Don't touch me!

589
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:57,460
I don't have
any bad intentions. I'm sorry.

590
00:38:57,960 --> 00:39:01,380
-And who are you?
-I'm Jerry Dimalanta.

591
00:39:01,464 --> 00:39:02,631
I want to talk to the mayor.

592
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:04,300
Have you scheduled an appointment?

593
00:39:04,967 --> 00:39:07,762
-No.
-Then you can't talk to him.

594
00:39:07,845 --> 00:39:11,140
And do I look like his secretary
who schedules his appointments?

595
00:39:11,849 --> 00:39:13,100
[sighs] Excuse me, mister.

596
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:16,228
We're not a church
that's open to everyone.

597
00:39:16,312 --> 00:39:17,313
We're busy!

598
00:39:17,396 --> 00:39:18,397
Yes, ma'am.

599
00:39:18,856 --> 00:39:20,775
Close the door! Close the door! Hurry!

600
00:39:30,951 --> 00:39:33,329
Mom, there's a change of plans.
I'm leaving this place.

601
00:39:33,412 --> 00:39:34,163
[Camia] <i>What?</i>

602
00:39:34,246 --> 00:39:36,415
What happened, dear?
What about your agreement…

603
00:39:36,499 --> 00:39:37,583
<i>with the Ardientes?</i>

604
00:39:38,209 --> 00:39:40,044
Arnaldo tried to kill me last night.

605
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:41,253
What?!

606
00:39:41,337 --> 00:39:44,507
I didn't see him,
but someone entered my room

607
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:45,883
<i>and tried to choke me.</i>

608
00:39:45,966 --> 00:39:48,511
And I know that it was Arnaldo.

609
00:39:48,594 --> 00:39:50,805
He's the only one who's capable
of doing that to me.

610
00:39:50,888 --> 00:39:53,099
[Camia] <i>That bastard.</i>

611
00:39:53,182 --> 00:39:54,767
You made the right choice.

612
00:39:54,850 --> 00:39:58,104
Get away from him.
Just come back here, Lily.

613
00:39:58,896 --> 00:40:00,689
Yes, Mom. Bye.

614
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:03,859
[suspenseful music playing]

615
00:40:12,576 --> 00:40:13,577
[ominous music]

616
00:40:19,708 --> 00:40:21,210
[dramatic music]

617
00:40:21,877 --> 00:40:24,004
Are you testing me, Arnaldo?

618
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:29,885
[ominous music]

619
00:40:41,021 --> 00:40:42,940
[suspenseful music playing]

620
00:41:00,124 --> 00:41:04,003
Hon! You came back! Perfect timing!

621
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:06,255
I am cooking your favorite.

622
00:41:07,715 --> 00:41:08,716
Steak for two?

623
00:41:12,219 --> 00:41:16,140
I know I'm a little rusty,
but I know how to prepare this.

624
00:41:16,223 --> 00:41:19,226
So, just relax. I know you'll love it.

625
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:20,436
Let me serve you.

626
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:22,855
-[sizzles]
-There you go.

627
00:41:22,938 --> 00:41:25,441
All right. Looks good.

628
00:41:30,070 --> 00:41:31,155
What's wrong?

629
00:41:33,949 --> 00:41:37,328
Oh! Wait! [chuckles] I'm really sorry.

630
00:41:38,204 --> 00:41:39,288
Wine!

631
00:41:40,206 --> 00:41:41,373
I almost forgot.

632
00:41:41,999 --> 00:41:46,795
Here you go. This is perfect with steak.

633
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:48,547
Here you go.

634
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:55,638
You go.

635
00:41:55,721 --> 00:41:57,598
-Okay.
-My tires are flat.

636
00:41:58,891 --> 00:42:00,893
It's like someone
doesn't want me to leave.

637
00:42:02,436 --> 00:42:03,521
Really?

638
00:42:03,604 --> 00:42:09,485
Well, maybe your tires
are worn out so they gave out.

639
00:42:09,568 --> 00:42:10,528
Don't you think?

640
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:13,614
[ominous music]

641
00:42:14,073 --> 00:42:16,242
Where are the nurses and maids?

642
00:42:18,953 --> 00:42:21,914
The nurses and maids? I got rid of them.

643
00:42:24,083 --> 00:42:26,877
You got rid of them? When?

644
00:42:27,962 --> 00:42:28,963
A while ago.

645
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:31,006
All of them?

646
00:42:32,132 --> 00:42:33,717
[chuckles] Yes.

647
00:42:35,010 --> 00:42:37,680
You told me someone entered your room.

648
00:42:38,305 --> 00:42:41,058
So, I thought, it's either the maids
or the nurses who would do that.

649
00:42:41,141 --> 00:42:42,726
So, they're all gone now.

650
00:42:43,561 --> 00:42:47,982
And besides, we don't need
the nurses because I feel good.

651
00:42:48,566 --> 00:42:50,734
I don't know why, but I just
really feel good today.

652
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:51,777
[stammers] I don't know.

653
00:42:51,860 --> 00:42:55,114
And we don't need the maids
because I can take care of you.

654
00:42:56,031 --> 00:42:57,032
Okay?

655
00:42:57,449 --> 00:43:01,203
Oh, and the bodyguards
won't be back any time soon

656
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:02,288
to accompany you,

657
00:43:02,371 --> 00:43:06,250
so I think you have
to cancel your meeting.

658
00:43:06,917 --> 00:43:07,918
Okay?

659
00:43:09,211 --> 00:43:10,212
Good.

660
00:43:10,838 --> 00:43:12,923
Okay. Perfect.

661
00:43:14,383 --> 00:43:15,384
Oh.

662
00:43:15,634 --> 00:43:16,719
Everything's set.

663
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:24,560
Cheers.

664
00:43:28,564 --> 00:43:30,566
[dramatic music playing]

665
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:36,572
[glasses clink]

666
00:43:46,832 --> 00:43:48,208
[Diego] <i>Just tell me if…</i>

667
00:43:48,292 --> 00:43:50,085
you need me, and I'll be there.

668
00:43:50,169 --> 00:43:55,633
No, Diego. I have to know
what's happening to Arnaldo.

669
00:43:56,216 --> 00:43:58,761
I have to know why he's acting strange.

670
00:43:59,219 --> 00:44:01,096
Ivy, please.

671
00:44:01,347 --> 00:44:04,141
It's too dangerous.
Arnaldo isn't thinking straight.

672
00:44:04,224 --> 00:44:05,517
Get out of there!

673
00:44:05,601 --> 00:44:08,395
Diego, I have to do this.
Let's talk again.

674
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:10,856
Ivy, please be careful.

675
00:44:11,857 --> 00:44:12,858
Thank you.

676
00:44:21,075 --> 00:44:23,035
[suspenseful music playing]

677
00:44:38,884 --> 00:44:40,010
[ominous music]

678
00:44:45,015 --> 00:44:47,851
[inner voice] <i>That was right.</i>
<i>You only did what's right.</i>

679
00:44:47,935 --> 00:44:49,770
<i>You were right to keep Ivy from leaving</i>

680
00:44:49,853 --> 00:44:55,067
<i>because she has to pay</i>
<i>for everything she did to you.</i>

681
00:44:55,567 --> 00:45:00,239
<i>She can't get away with it that easily.</i>

682
00:45:01,824 --> 00:45:05,577
<i>No, she can't. Never.</i>

683
00:45:07,121 --> 00:45:08,122
I love her.

684
00:45:10,165 --> 00:45:13,919
And, you know what? She loves me too.

685
00:45:15,963 --> 00:45:18,924
Okay? No. [scoffs]

686
00:45:19,633 --> 00:45:21,218
She loves me, and she couldn't

687
00:45:21,301 --> 00:45:22,970
do the things you're accusing her of.

688
00:45:23,053 --> 00:45:26,515
[inner voice laughing] <i>You are nuts!</i>

689
00:45:26,598 --> 00:45:27,891
<i>She doesn't love you! She's lying!</i>

690
00:45:27,975 --> 00:45:31,603
<i>She's only using you</i>
<i>and the rest of the Ardientes.</i>

691
00:45:31,687 --> 00:45:34,481
<i>But, since you're blinded</i>
<i>by your love for her,</i>

692
00:45:34,565 --> 00:45:36,608
<i>you can't see the truth.</i>

693
00:45:36,692 --> 00:45:40,070
<i>You can't see that</i>
<i>she's just putting on a show…</i>

694
00:45:40,821 --> 00:45:44,491
<i>so she can take revenge</i>
<i>on you and your family.</i>

695
00:45:44,575 --> 00:45:47,369
[stammering] What?!
What are you talking about?!

696
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:49,830
Revenge?!

697
00:45:51,081 --> 00:45:54,793
You don't know a thing!
You don't! You don't!

698
00:45:57,379 --> 00:45:58,172
You don't!

699
00:45:58,255 --> 00:46:01,758
[inner voice] <i>Really now?</i>
<i>But I know the truth.</i>

700
00:46:02,342 --> 00:46:04,511
<i>I've known this for quite some time now.</i>

701
00:46:04,595 --> 00:46:09,057
<i>Ivy Aguas and Lily Cruz</i>
<i>are the same person.</i>

702
00:46:11,560 --> 00:46:13,187
[ominous music playing]

703
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:18,484
[laughs]

704
00:46:19,443 --> 00:46:22,362
[Arnaldo] No! No, okay?

705
00:46:22,654 --> 00:46:24,990
You… You're not real.

706
00:46:25,449 --> 00:46:26,492
Okay?

707
00:46:26,575 --> 00:46:28,994
None of this is real. You aren't real.

708
00:46:29,912 --> 00:46:32,414
This is all in my head. See?

709
00:46:33,248 --> 00:46:36,627
I'm smart. I'm smarter than you.

710
00:46:36,960 --> 00:46:40,130
Okay? I won't believe you. No!

711
00:46:40,964 --> 00:46:41,882
No!

712
00:46:41,965 --> 00:46:43,759
[inner voice] <i>You know the truth, Arnaldo.</i>

713
00:46:43,842 --> 00:46:45,886
<i>I went to the mansion to see you.</i>

714
00:46:45,969 --> 00:46:49,139
<i>But, you killed me before</i>
<i>I got to tell you everything.</i>

715
00:46:49,723 --> 00:46:53,769
<i>You chose to kill me</i>
<i>instead of accepting the truth.</i>

716
00:46:53,852 --> 00:46:55,687
[Nimfa] <i>Mayor, you need to know</i>
<i>that Ivy is--</i>

717
00:46:55,771 --> 00:46:59,483
-<i>That's not true!</i> [screams]
-[gunshots]

718
00:47:02,986 --> 00:47:04,863
[dramatic music playing]

719
00:47:04,947 --> 00:47:06,949
You have no proof, okay?

720
00:47:07,449 --> 00:47:09,243
You have no proof!

721
00:47:10,619 --> 00:47:13,622
Unless you can prove everything
you're accusing Ivy of…

722
00:47:13,705 --> 00:47:17,960
I won't believe you. No! No!

723
00:47:18,043 --> 00:47:19,920
You're not going to ruin this for me.

724
00:47:20,003 --> 00:47:21,880
No! No!

725
00:47:21,964 --> 00:47:24,508
[inner voice] <i>Quit hiding from</i>
<i>the truth and start facing it</i>

726
00:47:24,591 --> 00:47:26,843
<i>before it knocks you down, Arnaldo.</i>

727
00:47:26,927 --> 00:47:29,888
<i>Open your eyes. Open them, and you'll see</i>

728
00:47:29,972 --> 00:47:32,641
<i>that there's only one way</i>
<i>to end your suffering.</i>

729
00:47:32,724 --> 00:47:33,976
<i>Just one.</i>

730
00:47:34,059 --> 00:47:35,602
<i>Kill Ivy Aguas!</i>

731
00:47:35,686 --> 00:47:36,687
No!

732
00:47:37,396 --> 00:47:40,732
[inner voice] <i>Kill her! Kill her!</i>

733
00:47:40,816 --> 00:47:41,692
You're insane!

734
00:47:41,775 --> 00:47:44,361
That's not going to happen, okay?

735
00:47:44,444 --> 00:47:46,363
That will never happen. Is that clear?!

736
00:47:46,446 --> 00:47:48,240
Never! Do you hear?

737
00:47:48,323 --> 00:47:51,493
Never! Never! Never!

738
00:47:51,577 --> 00:47:55,998
Never! Never! No! No!

739
00:47:59,209 --> 00:48:02,129
[dramatic music playing]

740
00:48:11,179 --> 00:48:14,558
[Julio] <i>He's really getting on my nerves.</i>

741
00:48:14,641 --> 00:48:20,731
<i>I am done trying to be good</i>
<i>and decent about this whole fiasco.</i>

742
00:48:20,814 --> 00:48:23,400
<i>I want you to bring me Diego Torillo.</i>

743
00:48:23,483 --> 00:48:25,986
<i>Dead or alive, it doesn't matter.</i>

744
00:48:26,069 --> 00:48:27,946
[Arnaldo] <i>What am I supposed</i>
<i>to do with this thing?</i>

745
00:48:28,030 --> 00:48:29,072
<i>Smash it on your head?</i>

746
00:48:29,156 --> 00:48:31,366
<i>Mayor, Mayor. I'm sure you'll give me</i>

747
00:48:31,450 --> 00:48:33,619
